Check environment configuration

Verifies that your environment is properly configured for Antithesis testing.
Runs health checks — container runtime, docker compose, the tenant and
repository settings, and your credentials (stored by `snouty login`, or set in
the ANTITHESIS_* environment variables). A missing tenant fails the check; a
missing repository is a warning, because only `snouty launch` needs it. doctor
also warns when more than one credential source is available. To see the
settings that snouty resolved, run `snouty settings show`.

snouty prefers an API key (full API access); a username and password is
deprecated auth, accepted only by `snouty launch` and `snouty debug`.

When credentials are configured, doctor also contacts the Antithesis API to
report the API and tenant versions and confirm connectivity. It warns when the
tenant release is too old for an API that some commands use, and when CLI OAuth
login is not enabled for the tenant. Pass --offline to skip these network calls.

The command fails if any required check fails. Pass --json for a
machine-readable report (e.g. to gate CI).

Examples:
  snouty doctor
  snouty doctor --json | jq .ok
  snouty doctor --offline

Usage: snouty doctor [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --offline
          Skip the network check (don't contact the Antithesis API for versions)

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

      --json
          Output JSON where supported (NDJSON for list/stream commands, pretty
          JSON otherwise)

      --verbose
          Log API requests to stderr (authentication tokens redacted)

      --settings <SETTINGS>
          Path to the snouty settings file (default: ./.snouty.toml; overrides
          SNOUTY_SETTINGS_PATH)

      --profile <PROFILE>
          Settings profile to select (overrides ANTITHESIS_PROFILE)
